    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="0904" n="1738" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/524b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-02T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1284. For Chadbourne, Smith [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 132. Consider very important to arrange that vessels not touching American
                    ports proceeding to Spain from South America, Central America, Mexico, West
                    Indies, etc., be compelled call at Porto Rico for examination to avoid necessity
                    Allied blockade fleet requiring vessels proceed Kirkwall or Gibraltar for
                    examination. Confidently reported Mexico assembling quantity Mexican coal at
                    Tampico to enable Spanish vessels proceed direct between Mexico and Spain for
                    frank purpose of evading our jurisdiction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
